00:06:15.333 --> 00:06:16.626
to the documentation 

00:06:16.876 --> 00:06:18.211
we know that Media Lab has 

00:06:18.211 --> 00:06:18.753
something called 

00:06:18.753 --> 00:06:19.754
an inspection proof 

00:06:19.754 --> 00:06:20.546
where you can upload 

00:06:20.546 --> 00:06:21.089
the checklist 

00:06:21.089 --> 00:06:21.964
that CAP provides, 

00:06:21.964 --> 00:06:23.257
which is super helpful 

00:06:23.257 --> 00:06:23.883
because it helps 

00:06:23.883 --> 00:06:24.592
to keep track of the 

00:06:24.592 --> 00:06:25.385
nitty gritty stuff. 

00:06:25.385 --> 00:06:26.844
Plus, the reason why people 

00:06:26.844 --> 00:06:28.262
like having an online system 

00:06:28.262 --> 00:06:28.971
is because you can have 

00:06:28.971 --> 00:06:29.847
all the documents 

00:06:29.847 --> 00:06:31.099
organized online 

00:06:31.099 --> 00:06:32.350
and stored in one place. 

00:06:32.350 --> 00:06:32.975
It's time to stay

00:06:32.975 --> 00:06:33.601
modern guys. 

00:06:33.601 --> 00:06:34.268
So instead of having 

00:06:34.268 --> 00:06:35.436
those tons of binders 

00:06:35.436 --> 00:06:36.062
with papers, 

00:06:36.062 --> 00:06:37.480
we highly recommend 

00:06:37.480 --> 00:06:38.106
that you check out 

00:06:38.106 --> 00:06:39.148
an online system. 

00:06:39.148 --> 00:06:40.358
Now, the next thing to cover 

00:06:40.358 --> 00:06:41.401
is a documentation 

00:06:41.401 --> 00:06:41.943
for training, 

00:06:41.943 --> 00:06:43.236
and I think you may start 

00:06:43.236 --> 00:06:43.986
to get an understanding of 

00:06:43.986 --> 00:06:45.321
what CAP is looking for, 

00:06:45.321 --> 00:06:46.614
but you want documentation 

00:06:46.614 --> 00:06:47.824
on everything. 

00:06:47.824 --> 00:06:48.533
The goal is that 

00:06:48.533 --> 00:06:49.242
you want to make sure 

00:06:49.242 --> 00:06:50.076
that all the lab 

00:06:50.076 --> 00:06:51.619
techs and anyone in the lab 

00:06:51.619 --> 00:06:52.745
performs processes 

00:06:52.745 --> 00:06:53.830
in a standardized way 

00:06:53.830 --> 00:06:55.123
and knows exactly what 

00:06:55.123 --> 00:06:56.582
to do with every scenario 

00:06:56.582 --> 00:06:57.750
and how to use each lab 

00:06:57.750 --> 00:06:58.709
equipment properly. 

00:06:58.709 --> 00:06:59.669
This means that they need 

00:06:59.669 --> 00:07:01.045
one document training 

00:07:01.045 --> 00:07:03.047
and then to a competent, 

00:07:08.344 --> 00:07:09.345
How do you say that word? 

00:07:09.345 --> 00:07:10.513
Competency assessment. 

00:07:10.513 --> 00:07:12.098
This is especially important 

00:07:12.098 --> 00:07:12.890
if you do multiple 

00:07:12.890 --> 00:07:13.516
kinds of tests. 

00:07:13.516 --> 00:07:14.392
For example, let's say 

00:07:14.392 --> 00:07:15.435
you do COVID testing 

00:07:15.435 --> 00:07:16.853
and then you also do gut 

00:07:16.853 --> 00:07:17.520
testing in your lab. 

00:07:17.520 --> 00:07:18.729
And let's say during COVID 

00:07:18.729 --> 00:07:20.148
19 that all the lab tests 

00:07:20.148 --> 00:07:20.731
were primarily 

00:07:20.731 --> 00:07:21.774
doing COVID testing. 

00:07:21.774 --> 00:07:22.984
They have a muscle memory 

00:07:22.984 --> 00:07:24.193
on the exact routine 

00:07:24.193 --> 00:07:24.569
since they've been 

00:07:24.569 --> 00:07:25.862
doing it for over a year. 

00:07:25.862 --> 00:07:26.737
But then someone 

00:07:26.737 --> 00:07:27.864
needs gut testing. 

00:07:27.864 --> 00:07:28.573
And what 

00:07:28.573 --> 00:07:29.532
we want to make sure is that 

00:07:29.532 --> 00:07:30.366
they could have 

00:07:30.366 --> 00:07:31.242
potentially forgotten 

00:07:31.242 --> 00:07:31.951
a step or two 

00:07:31.951 --> 00:07:32.952
during the gut testing 

00:07:32.952 --> 00:07:33.786
because someone needed it. 

00:07:33.786 --> 00:07:34.662
And that's the purpose 

00:07:34.662 --> 00:07:36.038
of the internal competency 

00:07:36.038 --> 00:07:36.539
to make sure 

00:07:36.539 --> 00:07:37.415
that the lab tech 

00:07:37.415 --> 00:07:38.666
can still perform a gut test 

00:07:38.666 --> 00:07:39.167
with the right 

00:07:39.167 --> 00:07:39.959
skills and knowledge. 

00:07:39.959 --> 00:07:41.127
So once you complete those 

00:07:41.127 --> 00:07:42.545
internal training documents, 

00:07:42.545 --> 00:07:43.504
you also need a place 

00:07:43.504 --> 00:07:43.838
to store 

00:07:43.838 --> 00:07:45.089
your personal documentation 

00:07:45.089 --> 00:07:46.215
for each employee. 

00:07:46.215 --> 00:07:47.175
This includes, at a minimum, 

00:07:47.175 --> 00:07:48.134
your education 

00:07:48.134 --> 00:07:49.469
degree, your resume, 

00:07:49.469 --> 00:07:50.761
a job description 

00:07:50.761 --> 00:07:52.054
and license if applicable. 

00:07:52.054 --> 00:07:53.097
Something to consider 

00:07:53.097 --> 00:07:54.599
is also having documentation 

00:07:54.599 --> 00:07:55.433
on how to navigate 

00:07:55.433 --> 00:07:56.309
your LIM system 

00:07:56.309 --> 00:07:57.351
and how to use it properly. 

00:07:57.351 --> 00:07:57.685
A LIM

00:07:57.685 --> 00:07:59.270
system is a laboratory 

00:07:59.270 --> 00:07:59.812
information 

00:07:59.812 --> 00:08:00.771
management system 

00:08:00.771 --> 00:08:01.814
which basically helps you 

00:08:01.814 --> 00:08:02.982
to effectively manage 

00:08:02.982 --> 00:08:04.525
samples and associate 

00:08:04.525 --> 00:08:04.859
the data 

00:08:04.859 --> 00:08:05.943
in an organized way. 

00:08:05.943 --> 00:08:07.278
Basically, you can easily 

00:08:07.278 --> 00:08:08.029
track the progress 

00:08:08.029 --> 00:08:08.779
of your samples. 

00:08:08.779 --> 00:08:09.489
It can also include 

00:08:09.489 --> 00:08:09.780
things like 

00:08:09.780 --> 00:08:11.032
tracking reagents, 

00:08:11.032 --> 00:08:11.449
tracking your 

00:08:11.449 --> 00:08:12.617
inventory management, 

00:08:12.617 --> 00:08:13.117
tracking your 

00:08:13.117 --> 00:08:14.243
sample management, 

00:08:14.243 --> 00:08:15.703
the process of the samples, 

00:08:15.703 --> 00:08:16.579
and even reporting 

00:08:16.579 --> 00:08:17.330
your results. 

00:08:17.330 --> 00:08:18.164
And finally, 

00:08:18.164 --> 00:08:18.831
you want to enroll 

00:08:18.831 --> 00:08:19.749
in a proficiency 

00:08:19.749 --> 00:08:20.750
testing program. 

00:08:20.750 --> 00:08:21.083
I know 

00:08:21.083 --> 00:08:21.876
CAP has a program, 

00:08:21.876 --> 00:08:22.543
but there's also 

00:08:22.543 --> 00:08:23.753
other programs like the 

00:08:23.753 --> 00:08:24.170
American 

00:08:24.170 --> 00:08:25.546
Proficiency Institute 

00:08:25.546 --> 00:08:26.506
where they send samples 

00:08:26.506 --> 00:08:27.507
with a known result. 

00:08:27.507 --> 00:08:28.132
And you just 

00:08:28.132 --> 00:08:28.716
want to make sure 

00:08:28.716 --> 00:08:29.300
that you can get 

00:08:29.300 --> 00:08:30.134
the same results 

00:08:30.134 --> 00:08:31.302
as them to verify 

00:08:31.302 --> 00:08:32.386
that your testing 

00:08:32.386 --> 00:08:33.137
is accurate. 

00:08:33.137 --> 00:08:34.138
Because if it's not done 

00:08:34.138 --> 00:08:35.264
well, that's going 

00:08:35.264 --> 00:08:36.474
to be a huge red flag 

00:08:36.474 --> 00:08:37.266
that some parts of 

00:08:37.266 --> 00:08:37.683
your testing 

00:08:37.683 --> 00:08:38.434
may not be right. 

00:08:38.434 --> 00:08:39.143
And once you 

00:08:39.143 --> 00:08:40.436
finish all of that, 

00:08:40.436 --> 00:08:41.103
then you wait 

00:08:41.103 --> 00:08:42.396
the onsite inspection day. 

00:08:42.396 --> 00:08:42.980
They'll be using 

00:08:42.980 --> 00:08:43.523
the same 

00:08:43.523 --> 00:08:44.482
customized checklist. 

00:08:44.482 --> 00:08:45.024
So there should be 

00:08:45.024 --> 00:08:46.400
no surprises and 

00:08:46.400 --> 00:08:47.735
you will receive a copy 

00:08:47.735 --> 00:08:49.278
of their report at the end. 

00:08:49.278 --> 00:08:49.737
So if 

00:08:49.737 --> 00:08:50.988
there are any deficiencies 

00:08:50.988 --> 00:08:51.739
or some things that 

00:08:51.739 --> 00:08:52.740
you may have missed 

00:08:52.740 --> 00:08:53.616
then you have 30 days 

00:08:53.616 --> 00:08:54.033
to respond 

00:08:54.033 --> 00:08:55.159
to any deficiencies, 

00:08:55.159 --> 00:08:56.327
they will then review 

00:08:56.327 --> 00:08:57.161
your application 

00:08:57.161 --> 00:08:58.663
and hopefully you'll receive 

00:08:58.663 --> 00:08:58.996
a CAP 

00:08:58.996 --> 00:09:00.289
accreditation certificate 

00:09:00.289 --> 00:09:00.831
by mail

00:09:00.831 --> 00:09:01.916
to the lab director. 

00:09:01.916 --> 00:09:02.416
You're basically 

00:09:02.416 --> 00:09:03.334
at the finish line. 

00:09:03.334 --> 00:09:04.210
The last thing you want 

00:09:04.210 --> 00:09:04.460
to do is 

00:09:04.460 --> 00:09:05.503
you want to maintain 

00:09:05.503 --> 00:09:06.504
this CAP accreditation 

00:09:06.504 --> 00:09:07.755
after all the hard work 

00:09:07.755 --> 00:09:08.089
you did, 

00:09:08.089 --> 00:09:09.131
and you just want to 

00:09:09.131 --> 00:09:10.675
perform self-inspection 

00:09:10.675 --> 00:09:11.217
and just make sure 

00:09:11.217 --> 00:09:12.385
that you maintain compliance 

00:09:12.385 --> 00:09:13.386
so that you don't lose it. 

00:09:13.386 --> 00:09:14.387
So that's the overview, 

00:09:14.387 --> 00:09:15.346
creating documentation 

00:09:15.346 --> 00:09:16.180
for every single 

00:09:16.180 --> 00:09:16.973
thing in your lab 

00:09:16.973 --> 00:09:17.932
and following it. 

00:09:17.932 --> 00:09:18.808
If you like this video, 

00:09:18.808 --> 00:09:19.225
be sure to 

00:09:19.225 --> 00:09:20.226
like and subscribe 

00:09:20.226 --> 00:09:21.519
to this channel. peace out.

